/-!
# The theorem on formal functions for algebraic spaces

In Situation 08AV — a Noetherian ring `A` with an ideal `I`, a proper algebraic space
`f : X ⟶ Spec A` and a coherent `𝒪_X`-module `ℱ` — fix `p ≥ 0` and write

* `M = H^p(X, ℱ)`, an `A`-module through `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.baseRingHom`;
* `M n = H^p(X, ℱ / I^n ℱ)`, the `n`-th term of the tower, the transition maps being the
  cohomology of the exponent-lowering maps.

[Stacks, Tag 08AZ] says that the maps `M / I^n M ⟶ M n` assemble into an isomorphism
`M^∧_I ≅ lim_n M n`, and moreover that it is a homeomorphism for the limit topologies.

The isomorphism is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.formalFunctionsEquiv`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.formalFunctionsEquiv_proj_of` says that it is
*the* map assembled from the projections: its `n`-th component takes the image of `x ∈ M` to the
image of `x` in `M n`.

## What is proved and what is carried

[Stacks, Tag 08AZ] has two clauses. Only the first, the isomorphism of `A`-modules, is treated
here; the second, that the comparison is a homeomorphism for the limit topologies, is **not**
proved and no declaration below claims it.

The isomorphism is proved granted the two clauses of [Stacks, Tag 08AY] that the source's proof
uses, carried as the named hypotheses `h08AY_ker` and `h08AY_range`:

* `h08AY_ker` is clause (1) of [Stacks, Tag 08AY]: for a fixed `c` and all `n ≥ c` the kernel of
  `M ⟶ M n` lies in `I^(n-c) M`;
* `h08AY_range` is clause (3): for every `n` there is a level `c₂ ≥ n` such that for all
  `k ≥ c₂` the image of `M k ⟶ M n` equals the image of `M ⟶ M n`.  The level depends on `n`,
  as in the source; it is not tied to the shift `c` of clause (1).

Clause (2) of [Stacks, Tag 08AY], the Mittag-Leffler condition, is not needed: in this
formulation it is subsumed by clause (3). The standing hypotheses of Situation 08AV — `A`
Noetherian, `f` proper, `ℱ` coherent — are what make [Stacks, Tag 08AY] true and are used
nowhere else in the argument; they are nonetheless genuinely present, being fields of
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation`.

Everything else is proved: the tower `n ↦ ℱ / I^n ℱ` and its transition maps are constructed,
`I^n` is shown to annihilate `H^p(X, ℱ / I^n ℱ)`, and the passage from those facts to the
comparison isomorphism is
`Stacks.IntertwinedFiltration.adicCompletionEquivTowerLimitOfEventualRange`, the source's own
argument carried out abstractly for a tower of modules over a commutative ring.

## Tagged declarations

Four declarations carry `@[stacks 08AZ]`, two for each of the two assertions of the isomorphism
clause, once for an arbitrary site and once in Situation 08AV:

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteAdicCohomology.adicCompletionEquivCohomologyTower` — the
  isomorphism `H^p(C, ℱ)^∧_I ≅ lim_n H^p(C, ℱ/I^nℱ)` on an arbitrary site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteAdicCohomology.adicCompletionEquivCohomologyTower_proj_of` — that
  it is the map defined by the system of projections, on an arbitrary site.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.formalFunctionsEquiv` — the isomorphism in
  Situation 08AV.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.formalFunctionsEquiv_proj_of` — that it is
  the map defined by the system of projections, in Situation 08AV.

The homeomorphism clause carries no attribute anywhere, because it is not proved.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteAdicCohomology.adicQuotient`, `adicProj` and `adicDrop` — on any
  site, the quotient `ℱ / I^n ℱ` of a sheaf of modules by the subsheaf generated by the
  `I^n`-multiples of its sections, the projection to it, and the exponent-lowering maps.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteAdicCohomology.cohomologyAdicTower`, `cohomologyAdicTowerMap` and
  `cohomologyAdicProj` — the tower `n ↦ H^p(C, ℱ/I^nℱ)` of `A`-modules, its transition maps, and
  the maps to it from `H^p(C, ℱ)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteAdicCohomology.IsAdicCohomologyBound` — clauses (1) and (3) of
  [Stacks, Tag 08AY], bundled, as they are carried here.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.adicThickening` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.Is08AYBound` — the same quotient and the same
  carried hypothesis, in Situation 08AV.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteAdicCohomology.globalSmul_adicQuotient_eq_zero` — multiplication
  by a global function coming from `I^n` is the zero endomorphism of `ℱ / I^n ℱ`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteAdicCohomology.smul_cohomologyAdicTower_eq_zero` — hence `I^n`
  annihilates `H^p(C, ℱ/I^nℱ)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteAdicCohomology.pow_smul_top_le_ker_cohomologyAdicProj` — hence
  `I^n H^p(C, ℱ)` lies in the kernel of `H^p(C, ℱ) ⟶ H^p(C, ℱ/I^nℱ)`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.FormalFunctionsSituation.cohomology_eq` and `cohomologyTower_eq` — the
  cohomology used in Situation 08AV is `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.cohomologyOverBase`.

## Implementation notes

**The ideal sheaf is taken on global sections.** On an algebraic space the subsheaf `I^n ℱ` is
`Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.idealSmul` for the ideal of global functions generated by the
image of `I^n`, and the quotient `ℱ / I^n ℱ` is the cokernel of
`Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.idealSmulHom`. The alternative vocabulary
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerMultiple` and `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.idealPowerQuotient`
of `StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/CoherentAdicSystem.lean` cannot be used here: it is
stated for `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.Modules.{u, u}`, since the abelian structure of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/Spaces/ModulesAbelian.lean` is available only at module universe
`u`, whereas `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.cohomologyOverBase` lands in module universe
`max (u + 1) w`. The two never meet. The `idealSmul` vocabulary is stated at exactly the
universe of `Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.globalModuleCohomology`, and the abelian structure it
needs is the global instance `Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesAbelian`.

**Why the construction is carried out for an arbitrary site.** With the structure sheaf fixed to
be that of the small étale ringed site of the algebraic space, instance search for
`HasCokernel` on the sheaves of modules does not terminate inside its heartbeat budget: the
module universe `max (u + 1) w` of the situation is a `max` whose `max (u + 1) u u` part has
already collapsed, so the universe arguments of
`Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.moduleSheavesAbelian` are left as metavariables constrained only
by `max (u + 1) ? = max (u + 1) w`. Over an arbitrary site the four universes are distinct
variables and the same search succeeds at once. The situation-level declarations are therefore
thin specializations, in which the universes are given explicitly and no cokernel has to be
found again.

**Restriction of scalars.** `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.cohomologyOverBase` is the cohomology of
the small étale ringed site with its scalars restricted along
`AlgebraicGeometry.Space.baseRingHom`; `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.SiteAdicCohomology.cohomologyRes`
is the same composite for an arbitrary ring map into the global functions, so the two agree by
unfolding. The action of `α : A` on a cohomology class is by definition the action of its image
in the global functions, which is why the vanishing statements pass between the two rings
without a bridge lemma.

**Commutativity of the sections.** The ideal of global functions needs the ring of global
sections to be commutative, which is `Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.globalIsMulComm` once the
sections of the structure sheaf are known to commute. Sheaves of modules are indexed by a
`RingCat`-valued sheaf, where commutativity is not an instance; it is transported from the
`CommRingCat`-valued structure sheaf of the ringed site by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.mul_comm_ringSheaf`.

